---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ToolHero from '../../../components/tools/ToolHero.astro';
import ToolHowItWorks from '../../../components/tools/ToolHowItWorks.astro';
import ToolFAQ from '../../../components/tools/ToolFAQ.astro';
import ToolRelatedCTA from '../../../components/tools/ToolRelatedCTA.astro';

const today = '2026-06-13T00:00:00+00:00';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What is a z-score and why is it useful?',
    a: 'A z-score (standard score) measures how many standard deviations a data point is from the mean. It standardises values across different scales, making it possible to compare results from different tests, datasets, or measurements. For example, a z-score of +1.5 means the value is 1.5 standard deviations above the mean, regardless of the original units.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How does the Best Answer Hub Z-Score Calculator work?',
    a: 'Enter the raw score, mean, and standard deviation into the Best Answer Hub Z-Score Calculator. Select whether you are using population or sample standard deviation. The calculator instantly returns the z-score, corresponding percentile, and a plain-English interpretation. A step-by-step breakdown and interactive bell curve visualisation are also provided.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the z-score formula?',
    a: 'The standard z-score formula is <strong>z = (x − μ) / σ</strong>, where x is the raw score, μ is the mean, and σ is the standard deviation. The Best Answer Hub Z-Score Calculator also supports reverse-solving: find the raw score from a z-score (x = μ + zσ), find the mean from a z-score (μ = x − zσ), or find the standard deviation from a z-score (σ = (x − μ) / z).',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can the Best Answer Hub Z-Score Calculator handle negative z-scores?',
    a: 'Yes. A negative z-score simply means the data point falls below the mean. It is not an error. The Best Answer Hub Z-Score Calculator displays negative results clearly and explains them in plain language, including the corresponding percentile and what it means in context.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I know whether to use population or sample standard deviation?',
    a: 'Use population standard deviation (σ) when the dataset includes every member of the group being studied. Use sample standard deviation (s) when working with a subset that estimates a larger population. The Best Answer Hub Z-Score Calculator includes a toggle to select the correct mode and automatically adjusts the formula notation.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does the Best Answer Hub Z-Score Calculator show step-by-step work?',
    a: 'Yes. The Best Answer Hub Z-Score Calculator includes a "Show step-by-step" option that breaks down every arithmetic operation (subtraction of the mean, division by standard deviation, and rounding) so the entire process is visible for homework or exam review.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I see a bell curve visual of my z-score?',
    a: 'Yes. The Best Answer Hub Z-Score Calculator generates an interactive bell curve that shows the position of the calculated z-score on the normal distribution. The area to the left of the score is shaded, making it easy to visualise percentiles, tail probabilities, and how far a score is from the average.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I convert a z-score to a percentile?',
    a: 'Enter the raw score, mean, and standard deviation into the Best Answer Hub Z-Score Calculator. The tool automatically computes the z-score and converts it to a percentile using the standard normal cumulative distribution function. For example, a z-score of 1.0 corresponds to approximately the 84th percentile, meaning about 84% of values fall below this score.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the z-score for the 95th percentile?',
    a: 'The z-score for the 95th percentile is approximately <strong>1.645</strong>. For a two-tailed 95% confidence interval, the critical z-values are <strong>±1.96</strong>. The Best Answer Hub Z-Score Calculator includes quick-reference chips for these common critical values, as well as 90% (±1.645) and 99% (±2.576) confidence levels.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can the Best Answer Hub Z-Score Calculator find the raw score from a z-score?',
    a: 'Yes. Switch to "Find Raw Score" mode, enter the z-score, mean, and standard deviation, and the Best Answer Hub Z-Score Calculator computes the original raw score using the formula <strong>x = μ + zσ</strong>. Step-by-step work and interpretation are provided just like in the standard z-score mode.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What does a z-score of 0 mean?',
    a: 'A z-score of 0 means the data point is exactly equal to the mean. In a normal distribution, this corresponds to the 50th percentile. The Best Answer Hub Z-Score Calculator highlights this result and notes that the value sits at the centre of the distribution.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is a z-score above 3 or below −3 possible?',
    a: 'Yes. While values beyond ±3 are rare in a normal distribution (about 0.3% of data), they are mathematically valid. The Best Answer Hub Z-Score Calculator handles extreme z-scores and flags them as potential outliers when relevant, with an appropriate interpretation.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I calculate the z-score for a sample mean instead of a single value?',
    a: 'Yes. The Best Answer Hub Z-Score Calculator includes a "Sample Mean" option that uses the standard error formula <strong>z = (x̄ − μ) / (σ / √n)</strong>, where n is the sample size. This is essential for hypothesis testing and sampling distribution problems.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I print or export the calculation steps?',
    a: 'Yes. The Best Answer Hub Z-Score Calculator offers a PDF export feature that captures the input values, formula, step-by-step work, bell curve graphic, and interpretation. No account or signup is required.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does the z-score assume a normal distribution?',
    a: 'The z-score itself can be calculated for any dataset, but percentile and probability interpretations assume an approximately normal (bell-shaped) distribution. The Best Answer Hub Z-Score Calculator displays a normality reminder when results are generated, helping users avoid misinterpreting skewed data.',
  },
];

const steps = [
  { title: 'Choose your mode', description: 'Select whether to find the z-score, raw score, mean, or standard deviation. Toggle between population and sample standard deviation as needed.' },
  { title: 'Enter your values', description: 'Input the known values: raw score, mean, and standard deviation. The calculator validates inputs and warns about common mistakes.' },
  { title: 'Get instant results', description: 'See the z-score, percentile, step-by-step work, plain-English interpretation, and an interactive bell curve. Export to PDF with one click.' },
];

const seo = {
  title: 'Z-Score Calculator with Steps & Percentile (2026)',
  description: 'Free z-score calculator with step-by-step work, percentile conversion, and an interactive bell curve. Solve for any variable. No signup.',
  url: '/calculators/statistics-suite/z-score-calculator/',
  type: 'WebPage' as const,
  datePublished: today,
  dateModified: today,
  breadcrumbs: [
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Calculators', url: '/calculators/' },
    { name: 'Statistics Suite', url: '/calculators/statistics-suite/' },
    { name: 'Z-Score Calculator', url: '/calculators/statistics-suite/z-score-calculator/' },
  ],
  faq: faqs.map(f => ({ question: f.q, answer: f.a.replace(/<[^>]*>/g, '').replace(/\s{2,}/g, ' ').trim() })),
};

---

<BaseLayout seo={seo}>
  <ToolHero
    backLink="/calculators/statistics-suite/"
    backLabel="← Statistics Suite"
    badge="Free Tool · Statistical Analysis"
    title="Z-Score Calculator"
    accentText="with Steps, Percentile & Bell Curve"
    description="Calculate z-scores instantly with step-by-step work, percentile conversion, and an interactive bell curve. Solve for z-score, raw score, mean, or standard deviation. All calculations run in your browser, with no data sent to any server."
  />

  <!-- Calculator -->
  <section class="py-6 md:py-8" aria-label="Z-Score Calculator">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <!-- Left: Inputs -->
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5 md:p-6">
          <!-- Mode Selector -->
          <div class="mb-5">
            <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-bae-ink mb-2">What do you want to find?</label>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2" id="mode-tabs">
              <button type="button" data-mode="zscore" class="mode-tab px-3 py-1.5 text-sm rounded-bae-sm border border-bae-border bg-bae-primary text-white font-medium">Z-Score</button>
              <button type="button" data-mode="raw" class="mode-tab px-3 py-1.5 text-sm rounded-bae-sm border border-bae-border bg-white text-bae-ink">Raw Score</button>
              <button type="button" data-mode="mean" class="mode-tab px-3 py-1.5 text-sm rounded-bae-sm border border-bae-border bg-white text-bae-ink">Mean</button>
              <button type="button" data-mode="sd" class="mode-tab px-3 py-1.5 text-sm rounded-bae-sm border border-bae-border bg-white text-bae-ink">Standard Deviation</button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Population / Sample Toggle -->
          <div class="mb-5">
            <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-bae-ink mb-2">Standard deviation type</label>
            <div class="flex gap-3">
              <label class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-bae-ink cursor-pointer">
                <input type="radio" name="sd-type" value="population" checked class="accent-bae-primary">
                Population (σ)
              </label>
              <label class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-bae-ink cursor-pointer">
                <input type="radio" name="sd-type" value="sample" class="accent-bae-primary">
                Sample (s)
              </label>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Inputs -->
          <div class="space-y-4" id="input-fields">
            <div>
              <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-bae-ink mb-1" id="label-x">Raw Score (x)</label>
              <input type="number" id="input-x" step="any" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" placeholder="e.g. 85">
            </div>
            <div>
              <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-bae-ink mb-1" id="label-mu">Mean (μ)</label>
              <input type="number" id="input-mu" step="any" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" placeholder="e.g. 70">
            </div>
            <div>
              <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-bae-ink mb-1" id="label-sigma">Standard Deviation (σ)</label>
              <input type="number" id="input-sigma" step="any" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" placeholder="e.g. 10">
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Sample Size (hidden by default) -->
          <div class="mt-4 hidden" id="sample-size-field">
            <label class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-bae-ink cursor-pointer mb-2">
              <input type="checkbox" id="use-sample-mean" class="accent-bae-primary">
              Calculate z-score for a sample mean (use standard error)
            </label>
            <div id="sample-size-input-wrapper" class="hidden">
              <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-bae-ink mb-1">Sample Size (n)</label>
              <input type="number" id="input-n" min="1" step="1" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" placeholder="e.g. 30">
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Action Buttons -->
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-6">
            <button type="button" id="calc-btn" class="bg-bae-primary text-white px-5 py-2.5 rounded-bae-sm text-sm font-medium hover:bg-bae-primary-dark transition-colors">Calculate</button>
            <button type="button" id="clear-btn" class="bg-white border border-bae-border text-bae-ink px-5 py-2.5 rounded-bae-sm text-sm font-medium hover:bg-bae-border/20 transition-colors">Clear</button>
            <button type="button" id="pdf-btn" class="bg-white border border-bae-border text-bae-ink px-5 py-2.5 rounded-bae-sm text-sm font-medium hover:bg-bae-border/20 transition-colors hidden">Download PDF</button>
          </div>

          <!-- Critical Values Quick Pick -->
          <div class="mt-5 pt-4 border-t border-bae-border-light">
            <p class="text-xs font-medium text-bae-muted mb-2">Quick reference: Common critical z-values</p>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
              <button type="button" class="critical-btn text-xs px-2.5 py-1 rounded-bae-sm border border-bae-border bg-white text-bae-ink hover:bg-bae-primary-soft" data-z="1.645">90%: ±1.645</button>
              <button type="button" class="critical-btn text-xs px-2.5 py-1 rounded-bae-sm border border-bae-border bg-white text-bae-ink hover:bg-bae-primary-soft" data-z="1.96">95%: ±1.96</button>
              <button type="button" class="critical-btn text-xs px-2.5 py-1 rounded-bae-sm border border-bae-border bg-white text-bae-ink hover:bg-bae-primary-soft" data-z="2.576">99%: ±2.576</button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Right: Results -->
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <!-- Main Result Card -->
          <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5 md:p-6" id="result-card" style="display: none;">
            <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink mb-4">Result</h3>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4">
              <div>
                <p class="text-xs text-bae-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-1" id="result-label-1">Z-Score</p>
                <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-bae-primary" id="result-z">—</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="text-xs text-bae-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Percentile</p>
                <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-bae-primary" id="result-percentile">—</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="p-3 rounded-bae-sm bg-bae-primary-soft border border-bae-primary/20 text-sm text-bae-ink" id="result-interpretation"></div>
            <p class="text-xs text-bae-muted mt-3 flex gap-1.5"><span aria-hidden="true">ℹ️</span><span>Percentile and probability values assume an approximately normal (bell-shaped) distribution. For skewed data, interpret these figures with caution.</span></p>
          </div>

          <!-- Bell Curve -->
          <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5 md:p-6" id="bell-curve-card" style="display: none;">
            <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink mb-3">Normal Distribution</h3>
            <canvas id="bell-curve" width="500" height="220" class="w-full rounded-bae-sm border border-bae-border bg-white"></canvas>
            <p class="text-xs text-bae-muted mt-2 text-center">Shaded area represents the percentile (area to the left of the z-score)</p>
          </div>

          <!-- Step-by-Step -->
          <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5 md:p-6" id="steps-card" style="display: none;">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-3">
              <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink">Step-by-Step Work</h3>
              <button type="button" id="toggle-steps" class="text-xs text-bae-primary font-medium bg-transparent border-0 cursor-pointer">Hide</button>
            </div>
            <div id="steps-content" class="space-y-2 text-sm text-bae-ink"></div>
          </div>

          <!-- Initial State -->
          <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5 md:p-6 text-center" id="empty-state">
            <div class="w-12 h-12 mx-auto mb-3 rounded-full bg-bae-primary-soft flex items-center justify-center text-bae-primary text-xl">📐</div>
            <p class="text-sm font-medium text-bae-ink mb-1">Enter your values and click Calculate</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-bae-muted">The z-score, percentile, bell curve, and step-by-step work will appear here.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How to Calculate Z-Score -->
  <section class="py-10 md:py-14 border-t border-bae-border-light">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-bae-ink mb-2">How to Calculate Z-Score</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted mb-8">The z-score formula and a worked example.</p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-6">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-bae-ink mb-3">The Formula</h3>
          <div class="bg-white border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm p-4 mb-4 text-center">
            <p class="text-lg font-mono text-bae-ink">z = <span class="inline-block border-b-2 border-bae-ink px-2">x − μ</span> / σ</p>
          </div>
          <ul class="text-sm text-bae-muted space-y-2">
            <li><strong class="text-bae-ink">z</strong> = z-score (standard score)</li>
            <li><strong class="text-bae-ink">x</strong> = raw score (the value being standardised)</li>
            <li><strong class="text-bae-ink">μ</strong> = population mean (average of the dataset)</li>
            <li><strong class="text-bae-ink">σ</strong> = population standard deviation</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-bae-border-light">
            <p class="text-sm text-bae-ink font-medium mb-1">Reverse formulas:</p>
            <ul class="text-sm text-bae-muted space-y-1">
              <li>Raw Score: <span class="font-mono">x = μ + zσ</span></li>
              <li>Mean: <span class="font-mono">μ = x − zσ</span></li>
              <li>Standard Deviation: <span class="font-mono">σ = (x − μ) / z</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-6">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-bae-ink mb-3">Worked Example</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted mb-4">A student scored 85 on a test where the class mean was 70 and the standard deviation was 10.</p>
          <div class="space-y-3 text-sm">
            <div class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-bae-primary-soft text-bae-primary text-xs font-bold flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">1</span>
              <p class="text-bae-muted">Write the formula: <span class="font-mono text-bae-ink">z = (x − μ) / σ</span></p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-bae-primary-soft text-bae-primary text-xs font-bold flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">2</span>
              <p class="text-bae-muted">Substitute values: <span class="font-mono text-bae-ink">z = (85 − 70) / 10</span></p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-bae-primary-soft text-bae-primary text-xs font-bold flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">3</span>
              <p class="text-bae-muted">Subtract: <span class="font-mono text-bae-ink">z = 15 / 10</span></p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-bae-primary-soft text-bae-primary text-xs font-bold flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">4</span>
              <p class="text-bae-muted">Divide: <span class="font-mono text-bae-ink">z = 1.50</span></p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-bae-primary-soft text-bae-primary text-xs font-bold flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">5</span>
              <p class="text-bae-muted">Interpret: The score is <strong class="text-bae-ink">1.5 standard deviations above the mean</strong>, approximately the <strong class="text-bae-ink">93rd percentile</strong>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Z-Score Table -->
  <section class="py-10 md:py-14 border-t border-bae-border-light">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-bae-ink mb-2">Z-Score Table Reference</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted mb-6">Common z-scores and their corresponding percentiles and confidence levels.</p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-bae-card border-b border-bae-border">
              <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-bae-ink">Z-Score</th>
              <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-bae-ink">Percentile</th>
              <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-bae-ink">Left-Tail Probability</th>
              <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-bae-ink">Right-Tail Probability</th>
              <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-bae-ink">Context</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="text-bae-muted">
            <tr class="border-b border-bae-border/50"><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-mono">−3.00</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">0.13%</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">0.0013</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">0.9987</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">Extreme outlier</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-bae-border/50"><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-mono">−2.00</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">2.28%</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">0.0228</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">0.9772</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">Very low</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-bae-border/50"><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-mono">−1.645</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">5.00%</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">0.0500</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">0.9500</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">90% CI lower bound</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-bae-border/50"><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-mono">−1.00</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">15.87%</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">0.1587</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">0.8413</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">Below average</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-bae-border/50 bg-bae-primary-soft/30"><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-mono font-bold text-bae-primary">0.00</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-bold text-bae-primary">50.00%</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-bold text-bae-primary">0.5000</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-bold text-bae-primary">0.5000</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-bold text-bae-primary">Exactly average</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-bae-border/50"><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-mono">+1.00</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">84.13%</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">0.8413</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">0.1587</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">Above average</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-bae-border/50"><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-mono">+1.645</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">95.00%</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">0.9500</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">0.0500</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">90% CI upper bound</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-bae-border/50"><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-mono">+1.96</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">97.50%</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">0.9750</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">0.0250</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">95% CI upper bound</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-bae-border/50"><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-mono">+2.00</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">97.72%</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">0.9772</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">0.0228</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">Very high</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-bae-border/50"><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-mono">+2.576</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">99.50%</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">0.9950</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">0.0050</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">99% CI upper bound</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-mono">+3.00</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">99.87%</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">0.9987</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">0.0013</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5">Extreme outlier</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-bae-muted mt-3">Values are approximate. The Best Answer Hub Z-Score Calculator computes exact percentiles using the standard normal cumulative distribution function.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

